I've completed the full analysis. Here is the formal audit against the **testsmells.org 19-smell academic catalog**.

---

## Test Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 · **.NET 10** · **Integration test class** (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`)

Integration-test calibration is applied throughout.

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell #1)

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 96)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);   // path A
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);       // path B
}
```

**Problem:** The `if/else` means only one assertion path ever executes per run. If `loaded` is never a `PremiumUser`, the discount-rate check is dead code — a hidden testing gap.

**Fix — split into two explicit tests:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", 0.15m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One branch is likely never tested, giving false coverage confidence.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell #4)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertion — passes even if every Insert silently fails
}
```

**Problem:** The test exercises code but asserts nothing. MSTest marks it as passing as long as no exception is thrown — even if zero rows were actually inserted.

**Fix — add a meaningful assertion:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — coverage metrics look good but nothing is actually verified.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Sleepy Test (Smell #3) *(downgraded from High — integration calibration)*

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);   // hard 3-second wall-clock wait

Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Problem:** A fixed 3-second sleep makes the suite slower and introduces non-determinism — the delay may be too short on a loaded CI agent or needlessly long on fast hardware.

**Fix — poll with a timeout instead:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var notified = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(notified, "Notification was not sent within timeout");
}

private static async Task<bool> WaitUntilAsync(Func<bool> condition, TimeSpan timeout)
{
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow + timeout;
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (condition()) return true;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
    return false;
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI failures and a 3-second tax on every suite run.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Catalog)

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);            // which failed?
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);   // which failed?
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);  // which failed?
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);        // which failed?
```

**Problem:** Four assertions with no message parameters. When one fails in CI, the test runner reports only the assert type and values — you must read the source to understand *which property* was wrong.

**Fix — add discriminating messages:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be assigned by the database");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slow diagnosis when tests fail in CI — you have to open the source to find which assertion broke.

---

### Smells Scanned — No Findings (Clean)

The remaining **15 smells** from the catalog were checked and are clean:

| Smell | Status | Notes |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | In-memory SQLite (`:memory:`) is hermetic — no external resource coupling |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | No test calls 4+ distinct production methods |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean | `3` and `10` in count assertions are self-documenting (items just added) |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean | No `.ToString()` comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` blocks |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean | Both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by all 8 tests |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` attributes |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean | No duplicated assertions |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean | Tests sharing `GetByEmail` each verify distinct behaviors |
| Constructor Init | ✅ Clean | Properly uses `[TestInitialize]` |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean | Meaningful class name |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean | No `Console.WriteLine` |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean | No tautological assertions |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean | Fresh in-memory DB each test |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean | No empty method bodies |

### Well-Designed Patterns Worth Noting

- **Test isolation** is excellent — each test gets a fresh in-memory SQLite database via `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]`.
- **Naming** follows a clear `Method_Scenario` convention.
- **`InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity`** is a well-constructed concurrency test with a proper assertion.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** — `BulkInsert` | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` | 🟢 2 min |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** — `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` | Split into two typed tests | 🟡 10 min |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** — `NotifyOnInsert` | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll loop | 🟡 15 min |
| 4 | **Assertion Roulette** — `InsertUser` | Add message strings to 4 asserts | 🟢 2 min |

Fix #1 and #4 first — they're two-minute wins that eliminate a false-pass risk and improve CI diagnostics. Then tackle #2 and #3 for correctness and reliability.
